ral footprint of the moon Io.)/Alt(A Hubble Space Telescope ultraviolet image of Jupiters complex, glowing aurora. The bright spot with a curving tail at the right is the auroral footprint of the moon Io.)/K 9/P 285 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/S/Figure>>endobj200 0 obj<</A 332 0 R/ActualText(An artists rendering of Jupiters inner magnetosphere, showing magnetic field lines \(connecting the north and south poles\) and auroras, along with a region of intense radiation around the planets middle.)/Alt(An artists rendering of Jupiters inner magnetosphere, showing magnetic field lines \(connecting the north and south poles\) and auroras, along with a region of intense radiation around the planets middle.)/K 6/P 285 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/S/Figure>>endobj201 0 obj<</A 333 0 R/ActualText(Illustration showing the relative distances of the planets from the sun)/Alt(Illustration showing the relative distances of the planets from the sun)/K 7/P 285 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/S/Figure>>endobj198 0 obj<</A 334 0 R/K 3/P 285 0 R/Pg 10 0 R/S/Span>>endobj278 0 obj<</K[220 0 R 222 0 R 224 0 R 226 0 R 228 0 R 232 0 R]/P 285 0 R/S/Story>>endobj279 0 obj<</K[233 0 R 237 0 R 239 0 R]/P 285 0 R/S/Story>>endobj280 0 obj<</K[241 0 R 242 0 R 282 0 R]/P 285 0 R/S/Story>>endobj276 0 obj<</K[204 0 R 205 0 R 216 0 R]/P 285 0 R/S/Story>>endobj282 0 obj<</C/Pa3+10/K[262 0 R 263 0 R]/P 280 0 R/S/Body_Text>>endobj334 0 obj<</LineHeight 8.0/O/Layout>>endobj10 0 obj<</ArtBox[0.0 0.0 792.0 612.0]/BleedBox[0.0 0.0 792.0 612.0]/Contents 335 0 R/CropBox[0.0 0.0 792.0 612.0]/Group 336 0 R/MediaBox[0.0 0.0 792.0 612.0]/Parent 3 0 R/Resources<</ColorSpace<</CS0 292 0 R>>/ExtGState<</GS0 294 0 R/GS1 293 0 R/GS2 337 0 R>>/Font<</T1_0 338 0 R/T1_1 295 0 R/T1_2 339 0 R/T1_3 340 0 R/T1_4 296 0 R>>/ProcSet[/PDF/Text/ImageC]/Properties<</MC0 341 0 R/MC1 342 0 R>>/Shading<</Sh0 343 0 R/Sh1 344 0 R/Sh10 345 0 R/Sh2 346 0 R/Sh3 347 0 R/Sh4 348 0 R/Sh5 349 0 R/Sh6 350 0 R/Sh7 351 0 R/Sh8 352 0 R/Sh9 353 0 R>>/XObject<